implementationPlan.description:
Preconditions and spelling inventory. Read-only: no tracked file changes.

WHERE YOU WORK. Read `get_context.workspace.mode`. Expect `worktree`, because this row's dependsOn chain runs through the worktree switch (flip gate task-6519ed9127ad4c359fd64b71f1a08be5, then WT-10M, then WT-14).
- In worktree mode your cwd is your task worktree: `$MOE_WORKTREE_PATH` = `.worktrees/<taskId>`, on `moe/task/<taskId>`.
- Every path in this plan is relative to `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, which is that worktree. Edit only those copies, with the Edit tool.
- NEVER write /mnt/d/projexts/moes/<file>. That is the control checkout: the wrapper reports such edits as MOE_WORKTREE_STRAY_EDIT and never lands them.
- In shared mode, work in the project root as usual.

PREREQUISITES. These docs describe behaviour from these rows, all upstream of this one:
- WT-10 (task-5c2e6cdf2494412ca0c2bc40e26d9da3), WT-11 (task-dd1ee586b90d4fc785434454b1423e76), WT-12 (task-06910296f63b4868849dc46cbb38a731), WT-13 (task-fbe8e3880ddf47dfa8546f220acea770);
- 31187ec1 (task-31187ec10ae54dd2b03f4c166f083f31), WT-10M (task-253884005a59471fb7c59ef38e1f3cc1), WT-14 (task-befdddf7e1f047a0ba4f71dd900c9b8f).
For each one, `git log HEAD --all-match --grep 'Moe-Task: <full id>' --grep 'Moe-Kind: completion' --format=%h -1` must print a sha.
- A row that was ARCHIVED instead is not an error; leave its behaviour out. The human may drop WT-10M, because this repo switched without the migration.
- A DONE row with no completion on HEAD: call moe.report_blocked with blockedOnTaskIds [that id] and stop.

INVENTORY. Write it to a scratch file outside the checkout (`mktemp -d`). The landed code wins over docs/plans/2026-10-30-per-task-worktrees.md.
- Codes and env vars, from `git show HEAD:scripts/moe-agent.sh` and `HEAD:scripts/moe-agent.ps1`:
  - every code and env var of the worktree arms, at least everything `grep -oE 'MOE_(WORKTREE|LAND|CONTROL|BOARD|PUSH|MIGRATION)_[A-Z0-9_]*[A-Z0-9]|MOE_WRAPPER_IN_WORKTREE'` finds (step 5 requires each one in the new scripts/CLAUDE.md bullet);
  - plus MOE_ATTR_EXCLUDED, MOE_CHECKPOINT_RECOVERED, MOE_COMMIT_NOTHING_TO_COMMIT, MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_{CONFLICT,GATE,LAND_LEASE,REF_CONTENTION} and MOE_RESCUE_REF.
  - For each, write one line from the code: what triggers it and what follows (the seat stops with report_blocked and no CLI, the unlanded route, or a warning only), and what moves and what never moves.
- Helpers and their twins:
  - sync_land_target / Sync-MoeLandTarget;
  - reconcile_push / Resolve-MoePushOutcome;
  - denied_wt (a python def inside moe-agent.sh) / Test-MoeDenyPathWorktree;
  - task_branch_landed / Test-MoeTaskBranchLanded;
  - control_worktree_mode / Test-MoeControlWorktreeMode;
  - gate_integrity_wt / Test-MoeGateIntegrityWorktree;
  - `run_frozen_gate worktree` / `Invoke-MoeFrozenGate -WorktreeMode`;
  - wt_land_rounds (3 rounds, 2 with a qualityGate);
  - plus whatever WT-11..WT-14 and WT-10M named for the unlanded route, the board snapshot, the control follow, removal and the sweep.
  - The design's take_unlanded_route, board_snapshot and follow_control_checkout are names to look for, not to copy.
- Refs, prompts and flags: moe/task/<taskId>, refs/moe/rescue/<taskId>/<utc-ts> and its reasons, refs/moe/board, moe/control, git-land-<target>, the LANDING-CONFLICT: and LANDING-RETRY: prompts, and --land-branch / -LandBranch.
- Daemon:
  - resolveWorktreeMode (state/validators.ts);
  - ExecutionAttempt.workspaceMode and AttemptWorkspace, and Task.landingRetry (LandingRetry, UnlandedReason), in types/schema.ts;
  - finalize_attempt outcome 'unlanded' (tools/finalizeAttempt.ts);
  - the complete_task worktree branch rule.
  Spell them as WT-17a's docs/MCP_SERVER.md and docs/SCHEMA.md do. If WT-17's docs/CONFIGURATION.md and WT-16's docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md runbook have landed, read them so nothing here contradicts them.
- This repo: `.moe/project.json` settings.worktreeMode and settings.consolidationBranch. On 2026-11-02 the human decided to keep main PR-only and land this repo on its consolidationBranch (the flip gate row).

Collect every design/code mismatch (a renamed, missing or extra helper, code or rule) for the completion summary and for one moe.add_comment on WT-19 (task-b1ca54f2716442be889a14623eb59983). A family code that HEAD mentions only in a comment goes on that list too. Never present a design-only name as shipped.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
Agents and humans reading root CLAUDE.md, scripts/CLAUDE.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md learn the worktree delivery path as the landed wrappers and daemon implement it:
- a per-task worktree on moe/task/<taskId>;
- one squash landing to the target (a literal consolidationBranch, else main), published by CAS or a non-forced push after the gate;
- the unlanded route and the LANDING-CONFLICT/LANDING-RETRY resume;
- board history on refs/moe/board and the control checkout on moe/control;
- removal and the orphan sweep, and the migration CLI if it shipped.
Shared-mode text stays intact, the daemon stays state-only, and no design-only name is presented as shipped.

acceptanceCriteria:
Every MOE_* token, Verb-Moe* cmdlet and backticked snake_case helper in the new text exists in HEAD's wrappers. These pass:
- daemonGitDocs.test.ts, in a clone snapshot;
- account-trust-docs.test.mjs;
- parity-check on HEAD's scripts.

invariants:
The safety negatives stay:
- never forced;
- no local-CAS fallback in remote mode;
- never auto-resolved;
- replay never re-lands;
- no unlanded commit is deleted without a rescue ref;
- the daemon never writes git state.

compatibility:
No code or contract change. Out of scope:
- docs/roles/* and packages/moe-daemon/src/generated/initFiles.ts (WT-18a, WT-18c);
- docs/MCP_SERVER.md, SCHEMA.md and CONFIGURATION.md (WT-17);
- docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md (WT-16);
- every .moe/ copy.

